### Step 2: `pages/reports-module/ExpenseReportPage.jsx` — NEW (~500 lines)

**File:** `/app/frontend/src/pages/reports-module/ExpenseReportPage.jsx` (NEW)
**Pattern:** EXACT clone of `DailySalesMockup.jsx` layout structure

```
Structure:
  ── Imports ──
  Sidebar, ReportLoadingShield, useReportFetch, InsightsCacheContext
  recharts (BarChart, PieChart, ResponsiveContainer)
  lucide-react icons
  expenseReportService (fetchExpenseReport, aggregateExpenses, etc.)
  exportReportAsExcel, exportReportAsPDF

  ── State ──
  isSidebarExpanded (default false)
  fromDate / toDate (from InsightsCacheContext)
  appliedFrom / appliedTo (triggers fetch)
  activePreset ('Today' | '7D' | '30D' | 'MTD')
  categoryFilter (null = all)
  paymentFilter (null = all)
  searchQuery ("")
  showDownloadMenu (false)

  ── Data ──
  useReportFetch → fetches raw data → aggregateExpenses → KPIs + charts + table

  ── Layout ──
  <Sidebar />
  <main>
    <ReportLoadingShield>
      ── Header: ← Back + "Expense Report" title + presets
      ── Date Range: From [___] To [___] [Apply]
      ── Filters: Category dropdown + Payment dropdown + Search
      ── KPI Strip (grid-cols-6):
        • Total Spend (₹)
        • Avg Daily (₹)
        • Transactions (#)
        • Active Days (#)
        • Top Category (name + ₹)
        • Highest Day (date + ₹)
      ── Charts Row (grid-cols-2):
        LEFT: Daily Expense Trend (BarChart — x=date, y=amount)
        RIGHT: Category Breakdown (PieChart — slices=categories)
      ── Payment Method Bar (single row):
        Horizontal stacked bar or cards showing Cash/UPI/Bank/Cash Draw
      ── Transaction Table:
        Columns: Date, Item, Category, Amount, Payment Method
        Sortable (click header), searchable, filtered
        Pagination or virtual scroll
      ── Download Menu: Excel / PDF / Email(disabled) / WhatsApp(disabled)
    </ReportLoadingShield>
  </main>

  ── data-testid attributes ──
  expense-report-page
  expense-report-back-btn
  expense-report-presets, expense-report-preset-{name}
  expense-report-from-date, expense-report-to-date, expense-report-apply-btn
